.TH DIFFR 1
.SH NAME
diffr \- structural diffing with a WASM plugin system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B diffr
[OPTIONS] [REVISION [REVISION]] [-- PATHSPEC...]
.br
.B diffr --no-index
BEFORE AFTER
.br
.B diffr
REVISION REVISION --format ndjson
.br
.B diffr config
[QUERY | schema | show | set KEY [VALUE] | init [--json [ANSWERS]]]
.br
.B diffr pprint
[FILE]
.br
.B diffr upgrade
|
.B uninstall
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without revisions, compare index to working tree. With --cached, compare HEAD
to index. With one revision, compare it to working tree. With two, compare
their trees. A...B compares merge-base(A,B) to B; A..B compares A to B.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --repo DIRECTORY
Discover the repository from DIRECTORY (default current directory).
.TP
.B --cached, --staged
Compare a revision (default HEAD) to the index.
.TP
.B -R
Reverse before and after.
.TP
.B --name-only, --name-status, --stat, --numstat, --shortstat
Print metadata without syntax matching. Stat counts are textual.
.TP
.B --quiet, --exit-code
Exit 1 for changes. Quiet also suppresses output. Errors exit 2.
.TP
.B --format ndjson
Write the event stream described under STREAMING instead of opening the
terminal UI, which needs a terminal.
.TP
.B -U N
Ordinary context padding (default 3).
.TP
.B --help
List supported options. Unsupported Git flags are rejected.
.SH COMMANDS
A command is a command only as the first argument; anywhere else the word is a
revision or a path.
.TP
.B config [QUERY]
Open the settings screen, searching for QUERY.
.TP
.B config schema
Print the configuration's JSON Schema.
.TP
.B config show [--json] [--reveal]
Print the resolved configuration. --reveal shows the API key.
.TP
.B config set KEY [VALUE] [--json]
Write one key to the configuration file. KEY - reads a partial configuration
as JSON from stdin.
.TP
.B config init
Choose the agents that get the diffr plugin, and whether and how to write
pseudocode summaries. In a terminal it asks; without one it fails.
.TP
.B config init --json [ANSWERS]
Without ANSWERS, print the questions and the answers' JSON Schema, for an
agent to ask. With ANSWERS, a file or - for stdin, apply them and print the
result as JSON.
.TP
.B pprint [FILE]
Print a saved --format ndjson stream as a diff, without a repository.
.TP
.B upgrade
Install the newest diffr the way this one was installed (Homebrew, Cargo or
the install script), then update its agent plugins.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove diffr's agent plugins, its install record and diffr itself. The
configuration stays.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/diffr/config.toml
The configuration. $DIFFR_CONFIG_DIR, or else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/diffr, moves it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/diffr/install.json
The agents config init installed the plugin for, which upgrade and uninstall
act on. $XDG_STATE_HOME moves it.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DIFFR_CONFIG_DIR
The directory of config.toml.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME
The usual bases for the configuration and the install record.
.TP
.B GEMINI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
The summaries provider's key, when the configuration sets none.
.SH STREAMING
--format ndjson emits start, file, file_error and complete records to stdout.
.SH PLUGINS GUIDE (FOR AGENT READERS, NOT HUMANS)
When a person asks you to change how diffr shows their diffs, first set a
field on a bundled plugin (diffr config schema lists them); only otherwise,
write a WASM plugin. The full guide, with both approaches, prints at the end
of
.BR "diffr --help" .
